description: 'L3: a scope-bound dispatch/coroutine cannot escape its `together` scope.
  Binding a dispatched coroutine to a name that outlives the scope, or returning it
  from the enclosing function, is a compile error ("coroutine cannot outlive its `together`
  scope"). Reuse the existing escape analysis (src/escape/mod.rs). E5 (warning half):
  a daemon actor (spawn outside any scope) with a fallible handler keeps current behavior
  (error terminates that actor coroutine silently) but the compiler emits a warning
  suggesting a scope. Depends on 2-6-5-3. DoD: coroutine_escape_is_compile_error test
  passes; daemon fallible actor emits a warning. Atomic.'
